Subject: RenderEngine: build the GPU context again after a GPU device loss

When the host GPU resets, the EGL display under SkiaGLRenderEngine answers
EGL_CONTEXT_LOST and Skia abandons a Vulkan context. RenderEngine aborted then: creating a
texture for a buffer, the device lost callback and the start of drawLayers all ended
SurfaceFlinger.

Before each use RenderEngine now checks for a lost device (Skia's context, or the EGL display
for GL). On a loss it drops its textures and Skia contexts while the old display still exists,
terminates and initializes the EGL display again (or makes new Vulkan devices), creates the
contexts again, waiting with backoff while the host GPU does not answer yet, and imports again
every buffer SurfaceFlinger has mapped. A frame drawn on a lost device reports DEAD_OBJECT
instead of a fence. getDeviceResetCount() and a listener tell SurfaceFlinger.

Applies to frameworks/native at ae266dcb706d083868578cfedce381ef44488a07 (Android 17).
